  "description": "45 The Broadway is a part single and part four storey commercial building located within Ealing Broadway. \nGround floor is currently utilised for Lloyds Bank - Use Class E(c)(i) with the upper floors providing office space ancillary to the existing bank. The application site totals 357sqm as highlighted by the red line on the application plans.\n\nUSE\nThe development seeks to convert first floor office accommodation to 1no dwelling whilst retaining the existing commercial use in the basement and on the ground, second and third floors respectively to form a mixed-use development.\n\nAMOUNT\nProposed schedule of accommodation is as follows:\nBasement | Use Class E (c)(i) @ 133sqm (as existing)\nGround | Use Class E (c)(i) @ 271sqm (as existing)\nFirst | Use Class C3 @ 86.1sqm (as proposed)\nSecond | Use Class E (c)(i) @ 105sqm (as existing)\nThird | Use Class E (c)(i) @ 55sqm (as existing)\n\nThe size of individual rooms within the proposed dwelling has been indentified on the relevant plans.\n\nLAYOUT\nThe arrangement of the dwelling utilises the existing footprint of the current first floor office accommodation with any alterations being made internally only. All of the habitable rooms as well as the dwelling as a whole complies with the local and national space standards.\n\nSCALE\nDue to the nature of the existing structure the dwelling will be well proportioned, particularly with respect to the ceiling heights and internal headroom. As the apartment has been designed in accordance with local and national space standards and best practice guidelines, the scale of the residential accommodation is appropriate for this size of the development.\n\nLANDSCAPING\nProposed development does not impact on the existing pedestrianised walkway (Oak Road). Since proposed works incorporate internal alterations only, no outdoor amenity space has been provided. However, it is noted that nearby public parks are located within 5-10min walk of the site.\n\nAPPEARANCE\nProposed development does not impact on the external appearance of the structure, therefore retaining the character and architectural of the building.\n\nACCESS\nThe development will utilise existing access points located off pedestrianised walkway (Oak Road). \n\nAppropriate measures will be put into place to ensure operational separation and management of the commercial premises to ensure the new dwelling can be accessed in a safe and secure manner. \n\nThe proposals utilise the principles of a car-free development in highly sustainable location (PTAL 6b) with excellent public transport links.",
